      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    X = np.load('vectors.npy', mmap_mode='r')  # (8000, 1024) float32\n    n = X.shape[0]\n\n    # Load into memory as float32 (8000*1024*4 bytes ~ 32MB, fine)\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Compute squared norms in float64 for accuracy\n    # sum of squares per row\n    sq_norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total = np.float64(0.0)\n\n    block_size = 500  # tune for memory/time balance\n    XT = X.T  # (1024, 8000), view, no copy\n\n    for start in range(0, n, block_size):\n        end = min(start + block_size, n)\n        block = X[start:end]  # (b, 1024) float32\n\n        # Compute dot products block @ X.T -> (b, n) using BLAS (float32 for speed)\n        dots = block.astype(np.float32) @ XT  # (b, n) float32\n        dots = dots.astype(np.float64)\n\n        # squared distances: ||a||^2 + ||b||^2 - 2*a.b\n        a_norms = sq_norms[start:end].reshape(-1, 1)  # (b,1)\n        b_norms = sq_norms.reshape(1, -1)  # (1,n)\n\n        sq_dist = a_norms + b_norms - 2.0 * dots\n        # numerical safety: clip small negative values to zero\n        np.maximum(sq_dist, 0.0, out=sq_dist)\n\n        dist = np.sqrt(sq_dist)\n\n        total += dist.sum(dtype=np.float64)\n\n    # total is a Python float via numpy float64; format as decimal\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.10f}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
